[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3745857515","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114930#issuecomment-3745857515","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114930","id":3745857515,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fRT_r","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-13T18:49:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T18:50:10Z","body":"> Consequently, `runnable` is no longer stored as part of the preset, but in a new section of `export_presets.cfg` called `runnable_presets`.\r\n\r\nDo we need to store this in `export_presets.cfg` at all? Like, it could just be temporary editor state stored in `.godot/`, like the saved size and position of windows.\r\n\r\nThe reason I suggest this is that I have a number projects with multiple presets for a single platform (usually Android, where each preset is for a different XR headset) and it's annoying to try and make sure that changes to which one is runnable don't get committed to the Git repo\r\n\r\nNot storing this in `export_preset.cfg` makes it so you can't save a \"default\" preset